/dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133373878,imgsize-807512.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nathan Cofnas faces ‘appropriate action’ from Ghent University after Arday’s death]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133373842.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/nathan-cofnas-the-scholar-who-exposed-jason-ardays-plagiarism-faces-appropriate-action-from-ghent-university-after-ardays-death/articleshow/133373842.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/nathan-cofnas-the-scholar-who-exposed-jason-ardays-plagiarism-faces-appropriate-action-from-ghent-university-after-ardays-death/articleshow/133373842.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T15:58:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133374002,imgsize-1744305.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[For over 50 years, Elizabeth Dickens recorded Block Island's birds, creating a historic record]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133372163.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[For more than five decades, Elizabeth Dickens kept a detailed account of bird sightings on Block Island. Her comprehensive journals offered insights into local bird populations and their migratory habits while she inspired students through educational efforts about avian life. Dickens' commitment to her craft resulted in invaluable contributions to ornithology, emphasizing how crucial careful observation is for comprehending the natural world.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1912-a-rhode-island-woman-began-recording-every-days-bird-sightings-on-block-island-she-continued-for-more-than-50-years-and-left-behind-one-of-the-islands-longest-wildlife-records/articleshow/133372163.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1912-a-rhode-island-woman-began-recording-every-days-bird-sightings-on-block-island-she-continued-for-more-than-50-years-and-left-behind-one-of-the-islands-longest-wildlife-records/articleshow/133372163.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133372236,imgsize-110389.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Carl Linnaeus: "Human beings, having, above..."]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133373633.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Human reasoning provides us with a special lens through which we can observe and understand nature. This ability to study and reflect upon natural processes imposes an ethical responsibility on us to avoid exploiting the environment. By grasping the intricate connections within ecosystems, we appreciate our place in the natural world. The wisdom of Linnaeus serves as a guiding light for today's pressing ecological issues.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/quote-of-the-day-by-carl-linnaeus-human-beings-having-above-all-creatures-received-the-power-of-reason-need-to-be-/articleshow/133373633.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/quote-of-the-day-by-carl-linnaeus-human-beings-having-above-all-creatures-received-the-power-of-reason-need-to-be-/articleshow/133373633.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T15:46:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133373852,imgsize-108736.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-origin man, woman arrested in Canada over alleged $6,000 extortion during date]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133372877.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/indian-origin-man-woman-arrested-in-canada-over-alleged-6000-extortion-during-date/articleshow/133372877.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/indian-origin-man-woman-arrested-in-canada-over-alleged-6000-extortion-during-date/articleshow/133372877.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T15:23:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133373076,imgsize-481140.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australian farmer spent three decades restoring land he once cleared; 24 bird species now live there]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133371396.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[About three decades ago, King Island farmer Fred Perry began changing the way he managed his land after his children urged him to protect the environment. Once known for clearing native vegetation, Perry and his wife Shona began fencing and replanting parts of their farm. The long-running effort has restored habitat and brought 24 bird species to the property year-round.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/about-30-years-ago-an-australian-farmer-began-restoring-land-he-had-once-cleared-after-his-children-told-him-to-protect-nature-today-24-bird-species-live-on-his-farm-year-round/articleshow/133371396.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/about-30-years-ago-an-australian-farmer-began-restoring-land-he-had-once-cleared-after-his-children-told-him-to-protect-nature-today-24-bird-species-live-on-his-farm-year-round/articleshow/133371396.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T15:08:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133372633,imgsize-120018.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists create a ‘laundry gun’ that kills microbes on astronauts’ clothes without water]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133371961.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-create-a-laundry-gun-that-kills-microbes-on-astronauts-clothes-without-water-paving-the-way-for-mars-missions/articleshow/133371961.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-create-a-laundry-gun-that-kills-microbes-on-astronauts-clothes-without-water-paving-the-way-for-mars-missions/articleshow/133371961.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T14:39:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133372141,imgsize-515854.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists discovered four snakes curled together in a burrow for 38 million years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133370865.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discovered-four-snakes-curled-together-in-a-burrow-for-38-million-years-as-the-volcanic-ash-preserved-their-remarkable-fossils/articleshow/133370865.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discovered-four-snakes-curled-together-in-a-burrow-for-38-million-years-as-the-volcanic-ash-preserved-their-remarkable-fossils/articleshow/133370865.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T14:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133370865,imgsize-120145.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[EDP445 in trouble as Kern County DA re-examines 2021 "cupcake" incident after new documentary]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133372204.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[EDP445 is facing renewed scrutiny after the Kern County District Attorney’s Office reportedly re-examined his 2021 “cupcake” incident following statements featured in Mike Clum’s documentary. The sheriff’s office says it is not actively investigating unless new information emerges. An extended documentary clip also shows Moreland discussing Jeffrey Epstein, Jared Fogle, R Kelly and Michael Jackson.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/edp445-controversy-returns-as-kern-county-da-re-examines-2021-cupcake-incident-after-new-documentary/articleshow/133372204.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/edp445-controversy-returns-as-kern-county-da-re-examines-2021-cupcake-incident-after-new-documentary/articleshow/133372204.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T14:48:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133372416,imgsize-83366.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[As 30% of Japan's temples risk disappearance by 2040, monks are using AI to help people speak with Buddha]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133371560.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[By 2040, Japanese temples may face closure due to dwindling religious commitment among the populace. In a bid to attract more visitors spiritually, monks are embracing artificial intelligence to improve operational efficiency and enhance communication with worshippers. While some view AI as a useful guide in matters of faith, others argue that the essential human connection is irreplaceable.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/as-30-of-japans-temples-risk-disappearance-by-2040-monks-are-using-ai-to-help-people-speak-with-buddha/articleshow/133371560.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/as-30-of-japans-temples-risk-disappearance-by-2040-monks-are-using-ai-to-help-people-speak-with-buddha/articleshow/133371560.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T14:21:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133371590,imgsize-117242.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Doctors gave Seattle shipbuilder months to live; he sold his business, moved to an island and lived another 38 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133371369.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Robert Moran, Seattle's former mayor, made a monumental gift of thousands of acres for a state park. Following a serious illness, he relocated to Orcas Island, where he developed picturesque forest lands into a personal estate. His visionary donation led to the establishment of Washington's first state park, named Moran State Park in his honor, which remains a beloved destination to this day.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1905-doctors-told-a-seattle-shipbuilder-he-had-only-months-to-live-he-sold-his-business-for-3-5-million-moved-to-an-island-gave-nearly-2700-acres-away-and-lived-another-38-years/articleshow/133371369.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1905-doctors-told-a-seattle-shipbuilder-he-had-only-months-to-live-he-sold-his-business-for-3-5-million-moved-to-an-island-gave-nearly-2700-acres-away-and-lived-another-38-years/articleshow/133371369.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T14:16:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133371400,imgsize-55956.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[18-year-old Texas student trains da Vinci robot to remove tumours; succeeds in 3 of 4 tests]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133370318.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A brilliant eighteen-year-old student has engineered a cutting-edge framework designed for surgical robots. Utilizing a simulation strategy, this innovative system instructs robots on autonomous tumor excision. Tested on a da Vinci surgical platform alongside gel models, it achieved success by removing tumors in three out of four trials. This pioneering research paves the way for the future of medical robotics.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-rayhan-papar-the-18-year-old-texas-student-who-trained-a-da-vinci-surgical-robot-to-remove-tumors-it-succeeded-in-3-of-4-gel-model-tests/articleshow/133370318.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-rayhan-papar-the-18-year-old-texas-student-who-trained-a-da-vinci-surgical-robot-to-remove-tumors-it-succeeded-in-3-of-4-gel-model-tests/articleshow/133370318.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T14:02:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133370515,imgsize-1813898.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Manhattan’s traffic-packed Broadway is slowly becoming a 5-mile wildlife corridor]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133368192.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Manhattan’s Broadway medians are being replanted with native Northeast species under a long-term project by the Broadway Mall Association. The Great Green Way covers five miles of Broadway and aims to connect 83 green malls into a corridor that can support birds, bees and other wildlife. Twelve malls have been restored so far, with more planting planned through 2026.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/between-six-lanes-of-manhattan-traffic-broadways-medians-are-being-replanted-with-native-species-to-create-a-five-mile-corridor-for-birds-and-bees/articleshow/133368192.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/between-six-lanes-of-manhattan-traffic-broadways-medians-are-being-replanted-with-native-species-to-create-a-five-mile-corridor-for-birds-and-bees/articleshow/133368192.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T14:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133370102,imgsize-201794.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Broxted Estate Solar Farm: biodiversity rises 41% in long-term study]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133365712.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-uk-solar-farm-began-generating-electricity-in-2013-12-years-later-its-biodiversity-had-rise